+# Daily Grind rewards
+
+Node.js 24+ serves the homepage and `POST /api/verify-email`. Install dependencies with `pnpm install`. `pnpm build` performs source/markup checks without importing the server or opening a listening port.
+
+Deployment requires:
+
+- `PUBLIC_ORIGIN`: exact public HTTPS origin, without a path. This controls the expected Origin and token audience; configure it explicitly behind a reverse proxy.
+- `EMAIL_VERIFICATION_ORIGIN_TRIAL`: a valid Chrome Email Verification origin-trial token registered for that origin. The server sends it on the homepage and form responses. Obtain it through https://developer.chrome.com/docs/identity/email-verification/verifier.
+- `DATA_DIR`: a persistent, writable volume for `rewards.sqlite` (default `./data`). Restrict access and back it up. The included SQLite deployment is for one service instance; distributed deployments need a shared transactional store for challenges and members.
+- `NODE_ENV=production` enforces HTTPS configuration. Terminate TLS at the hosting proxy. `PORT` defaults to 11222.
+
+The configured start command is `pnpm start`. No server was started during implementation.
+
+Each rendered form receives a fresh 256-bit nonce stored server-side under an opaque HttpOnly, SameSite cookie (Secure over HTTPS). Pages use `Cache-Control: no-store`. A POST atomically consumes its nonce before parsing the proof. Expired challenges are removed on page render. Multiple tabs retain independent challenge cookies only until another page render; an overwritten or consumed challenge produces a fresh retry form.
+
+The server validates DNS issuer delegation, HTTPS discovery, public network destinations, issuer keys and signature, expiry/freshness, email equality, browser key signature, audience, nonce and SD-JWT binding hash using `@sd-jwt/core` and `jose`. Network calls have time/size limits and no redirects. Verified accounts are persisted with a unique case-insensitive email key and terms version; duplicate submissions do not create another account. This creates rewards membership records, not a general sign-in/session system.
+
+Unsupported browsers, missing provider sessions, absent tokens, and invalid proofs receive an explanatory retry form. Per the requested email-free flow, no OTP or magic link fallback is sent and no unverified account is created. Actual verification requires a participating provider, supported browser, HTTPS and a valid trial token. There is no reliable generic JavaScript capability check for the hidden autocomplete extension; an empty token is handled by the server.
+
+The homepage keeps the existing menu, café, story, order and policy links; their destination pages are outside this change. Replace those destinations with your live pages, including the Rewards Terms, before launch. Photos are hosted by Unsplash.
